    {
      "body": "This PR has been automatically converted to **draft** because all PRs must start as drafts.\n\nWhen you are ready for review, click **Ready for Review** to begin the review process. This will:\n1. Add the oncall reviewer (optional reviewer)\n2. Add required review teams based on your changes\n\nSee the [contribution guide](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/docs/developer/submit.md) for more details.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-26T21:23:14Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/5001#issuecomment-4549035920",
      "id": 4549035920,
      "updated_at": "2026-05-26T21:23:14Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "github-actions[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hello @shurkat-nvidia, thanks for the distributed-init improvement and the checkpoint-time numbers.\r\n\r\nI checked the patch: it changes the default `DistributedInitConfig.distributed_backend` from `\"nccl\"` to the multi-backend string `\"cpu:gloo,cuda:nccl\"`, so both Gloo and NCCL process groups are created eagerly at `init_process_group()` instead of constructing Gloo lazily on first checkpoint use. The intended benefit is clear: avoid paying that Gloo initialization cost during the first checkpoint.\r\n\r\nThe main review question is compatibility: configs/types that assumed only `\"nccl\" | \"gloo\"`, plus environments where the multi-backend backend string is not supported. I'm assigned as current MCore oncall to route the distributed-init/training review and confirm CI coverage for that default change.",
      "created_at": "2026-06-05T16:30:38Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/5001#issuecomment-4633525858",
      "id": 4633525858,
